This patch documents the local ROCm workaround applied to
`site-packages/o_voxel/postprocess.py`.

Summary:

1. Add a CPU closest-point helper based on SciPy `cKDTree`.
2. Skip GPU `cumesh.cuBVH` construction when `OVOXEL_PROJECTION_MODE=cpu_kdtree`
   and `remesh=False`.
3. During texture baking, replace `bvh.unsigned_distance()` with CPU KDTree
   projection when `OVOXEL_PROJECTION_MODE=cpu_kdtree`.

The automated application is implemented in:

```text
scripts/apply-runtime-patches.sh
```

Reason:

`cumesh.cuBVH.unsigned_distance()` may fail on ROCm/gfx1201 with
`hipErrorIllegalState`. The CPU fallback is slower but allows textured GLB export
without using the unstable GPU distance kernel.
